  "title": "# Help mode: a switch that teaches Brett his own apps (Brett, Nov 1 early) Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/…",
  "asked": "# Help mode: a switch that teaches Brett his own apps (Brett, Nov 1 early) Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md, _claude/persona.md. Opus, one session. Git login works: plain `git push`. Brett: the system is getting deep. He needs a HELP MODE switch: when it's on, the app teaches him how to use it, with TOOLTIPS EVERYWHERE. Off = no tooltips, no clutter. Framework-level (framework/react + framework libs, so every app on AmberX gets it: console + all plugin pages, axhub-web, AmberX web, Patches, Walkthrough Studio): 1. The switch: a global 'Help mode' toggle in the app menu and top bar (a ? icon that lights up), plus a voice/keyboard shortcut. Remembered per device; also in Settings. Hot-swappable like everything else. 2. Help content as assets: help@1 asset type (framework/schemas + both validators + fixtures): id, target (control/screen id), title, plain-English text (what it does, when to use it, what happens if you tap it), optional 'try it' step, optional link to install_steps/docs. Written for Brett: short, plain, a little Amber attitude allowed, no jargon without a one-line explanation. 3. Tooltips everywhere: every framework control (buttons, menu items, toggles, sliders, grid columns, banners, cards, tabs) gets a stable help id automatically (derived from its action/command id or label). With Help mode on: hover (desktop) or long-press/tap the small ? badge (phone) shows the tooltip; tooltips never block the control; dismiss by tapping anywhere. 4. Screen intros: first time on a screen in Help mode, a short 2-4 step walkthrough of the main parts (skippable, 'don't show again'). Reuse Walkthrough Studio's format if it fits. 5. Coverage: write help assets for EVERY existing screen and control in the console and its plugins (Builds/Steps view, orchestrator, profiles, approvals + Approve now/Deny/who asked/expand/Watch live, UI Review + Screenshots + groups, Breakroom/agent swarm + HR panel parts already on main, banners, settings, terminal, keys, Plan Studio...) and axhub-web. Generate drafts from the code (labels, commands, READMEs, install_steps, reports) then edit for plain English. Missing help = a 'No help yet' tooltip + it's listed in a coverage report. 6. Coverage check in CI: script lists controls without help assets; CI fails if coverage drops below the current number (ratchet). Plugins get a manifest hook so new plugins ship their help with them. 7. Ask: a 'What is this?' button in a tooltip opens a small panel with the longer explanation and related screens. Framework controls + theme/scale tokens only; tooltip look comes from the theme. Phone-first. Tests: switch on/off, tooltip show/dismiss on hover + long-press, auto help ids stable, intro once per screen, asset validation, coverage script + ratchet. Full local test block from .github/workflows/android.yml + theme/controls/lifecycle/menu-reach checks. Screenshots (phone + desktop) of Help mode on several screens to UI Review via framework/cli/shot.mjs, group 'Help mode - Nov 1'. Add 'Part K: Help mode' to install_steps. Merge origin/main first; many builds are landing. Commit, fetch+merge origin/main, retest, `git push origin HEAD:main` (never force). Report at _claude/builds/reports/help-mode.md with coverage numbers. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault).",
